  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:5005",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through a series of interconnected pathways that ultimately lead to interactions with HCT-8 cells. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C targets multiple kinases, including ICK, which is inhibited by Ent-Gloeosteretriol. This inhibition, in turn, affects HCT-8 cells, as indicated by the downstream targets of Ent-Gloeosteretriol. Similarly, Oblonganoside C also targets Caov-4 and NCI-H1734, which are both inhibited by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, and both of these cell lines also show a target relationship with HCT-8. The consistent involvement of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a mediator across different targets implies a potential mechanism of action involving this compound. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central mediator in the signaling cascade initiated by Oblonganoside C, ultimately influencing HCT-8 cells through the regulation of key kinases.",
